Third-party contents of the `logweir-ui` image
==============================================

This image is built by `Dockerfile.ui` and carries exactly two things: the
fourteen static files of Logweir's page (Logweir's own code, Apache-2.0 —
/usr/share/licenses/logweir/LICENSE and NOTICE), and the base image below,
which it REDISTRIBUTES in full.

base image
  registry.k8s.io/kubectl@sha256:59bafa07ff3a6d4b417e7633ddb9d79a9606ca98bf64bac080b3e65748669250
  resolved from registry.k8s.io/kubectl:v1.34.1 on 2026-09-12
  (`docker buildx imagetools inspect registry.k8s.io/kubectl:v1.34.1`;
   charts/logweir/README.md records the command and the date)

what it contains
  /bin/kubectl — the Kubernetes command-line tool, and a distroless root
  filesystem. It is the process this image runs: `kubectl proxy --www=/ui …`,
  with every argument supplied by the Helm chart and none by this image.

licence
  Apache License, Version 2.0
  Copyright The Kubernetes Authors.
  Text: /usr/share/licenses/kubectl/LICENSE in this image (an unmodified copy
  of the Apache-2.0 text — the same licence Logweir's own code carries, which
  is why one file in the tree serves both paths). Upstream:
  https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/LICENSE

what this image does NOT carry, stated because an absent notice is a claim too
  * no `kafka-backup` binary and no OSO code — so no MIT notice, and
    /usr/share/licenses/kafka-backup/ is absent (`scripts/check-image-ui.sh`
    asserts it stays absent);
  * no Rust binary and no crate from Logweir's dependency graph — so no
    THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, which is that graph's inventory and would claim a
    redistribution this image does not make.

Kubernetes® is a registered trademark of The Linux Foundation. Apache Kafka®
and Kafka® are registered trademarks of the Apache Software Foundation.
Logweir is not affiliated with or endorsed by either.
